  "notes": "Guitar-rooted 2020s pop/hip-hop hybrid producer, usually working in a duo. The Lane line names the straight class first — \"backbeat on 2&4 straight for the pop-punk-facing work, half-time for the melodic-rap work\" — so this model is `backbeat_24` and the half-time half stays documented. The kit is the hybrid the entry describes: \"a programmed trap kick and 808 under a played or sampled rock backbeat, with 16th hats that drop out under choruses; claps layered on 2&4 for the pop-facing records.\" That is a hard-quantised kick against a jittered snare, `hihat.fillDensity` at 0.3 with a real roll vocabulary kept from the trap half, and a doubled clap stack. The low end is the axis signature and the entry states it precisely: \"808 sub with short glides sitting under a distorted electric bass; the two are frequently stacked, which is the signature low end of this axis.\" So `bass808` is `counter_riff` at `medium` distortion and the bassline is a `mirror_kick` distorted electric at a high `followRootsProb` — stacked, not alternating, which is why both follow the same rhythm rather than moving independently. Harmony is \"minor keys with pop-punk diatonic loops (i—VI—III—VII and i—VII—VI) and blues-third melodic borrowing; he began on guitar at ten … so the harmony is guitar-shape-derived\", which is those two families verbatim, a high `triad` share and `colorTones` on the flat third. \"Distorted and clean electric guitars as the primary chordal and melodic instruments over 4-bar minor loops; toplines are short-celled and shouted\" is the guitar timbre, the small `motifPitchCount` and the short runtimes in the arrangement. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says why: \"parametric detail inferred from those records and marked\". Every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 120 (the midpoint of the stated 90—150 band) are INFERRED.",
